  "title": "Peach Melba",
  "description": "If you're in a hurry or you don't have fresh peaches, just use canned peaches.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p> This is my version of a classical dessert \"Peach Melba\". You just need roasted peaches, a red berry sauce and an exquisite whipped cream. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21463,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1755295486789} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21463-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Peach Melba</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/IMG_2437.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tIf you're in a hurry or you don't have fresh peaches, just use canned peaches.\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>3 peaches</li><li>1 Tbsp brown sugar (or sugar)</li><li>250 g berries (raspberries, strawberries, blackberries)...)</li><li>200 ml heavy whipping cream ( 35%) (very cold)</li><li>2 tsp sugar</li><li>1/2 l vanilla ice cream</li><li>Some dark chocolate</li><li>Some sliced almonds</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Preheat oven to 390 degrees F. Line one baking sheet with parchment paper.</li><li>Cut the peaches in half, and remove the stones. Place the peach halves on the baking sheet. Sprinkle with brown sugar. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_2212.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Bake in the oven about 35 minutes until the peaches are tender. Remove from the oven, let them cool down completely, then carefully peel the skin.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_2217.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Rinse and drain fresh berries and puree them until smooth. Pass the puree through a fine sieve to remove all tiny seeds.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_2130.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Whip the heavy cream with the sugar until fluffy. Don't over beat. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/IMG_2430.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>In each glass, put one half of peach and one ball of vanilla ice cream.\r\n<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_2424.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Pour 2 tablespoons of berries puree.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_2427.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Add the whipped cream and finish with chocolate crumbs and sliced almonds. Serve right away. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/IMG_2435.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
